  "label": "User projected onto the textual message and visual scene",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'allah is watching you' and the visual scene of the woman pointing upward, as the phrase 'watching you' directly addresses the viewer ('you'), creating a direct semiotic projection where the user is positioned as the subject being observed. The visual scene reinforces this by mapping the gesture to the divine surveillance concept, making the user feel personally addressed and monitored.",
